spice-vdagent-wayland (0.23.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging-only release; no change to the agent itself, so the Debian
    and RPM packages are functionally identical to 0.23.1. The Arch
    package now installs spice-vdagentd to /usr/bin instead of shipping a
    real /usr/sbin/ directory, which conflicted with the /usr/sbin symlink
    owned by Arch's filesystem package and made 0.23.1 uninstallable with
    pacman. CI now installs the built Arch package to catch this class of
    failure before release.

 -- spice-vdagent-wayland <noreply@github.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:36:00 -0700

spice-vdagent-wayland (0.23.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix guest resolution reporting on a fractionally-scaled Wayland
    compositor: gdk_monitor_get_geometry() returns logical (scale-divided)
    pixels, not the physical pixels every consumer of this value actually
    needs (the real guest framebuffer, and absolute pointer positions a
    SPICE client sends). At any monitor scale other than an exact integer,
    this made the guest's on-screen cursor track proportionally wrong
    relative to the client's actual pointer position.

 -- spice-vdagent-wayland <noreply@github.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 01:33:59 -0700

spice-vdagent-wayland (0.23.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: fork of spice-vdagent adding native Wayland support.
    Clipboard sync (text and images, CLIPBOARD and PRIMARY selections) via
    wlr-data-control-unstable-v1. Resolution-setting via
    wlr-output-management-unstable-v1 (wlroots compositors) or
    org.gnome.Mutter.DisplayConfig (GNOME) -- both unimplemented under
    Wayland in the official package.

 -- spice-vdagent-wayland <noreply@github.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 00:19:09 -0700
